const lectD=[{title:"AI in Healthcare",text:"Good morning. Today I'll discuss how AI is transforming healthcare. Deep learning algorithms can detect early signs of cancer in X-rays and MRI scans, sometimes more accurately than human radiologists. These systems train on thousands of medical images, learning patterns invisible to the human eye. Another application is drug discovery: traditional development takes twelve years and costs billions. AI can simulate molecular interactions, predicting which compounds work, reducing time and cost. However, patient data privacy remains a major concern. AI needs large datasets, but this data is extremely sensitive. We need robust frameworks protecting information while allowing innovation.",q:[{qt:"What can deep learning detect?",o:["Patient names","Early cancer signs","Hospital locations","Equipment failures"],c:1,fb:"Detecta signos tempranos de cancer."},{qt:"How long does drug development take?",o:["5 years","8 years","12 years","20 years"],c:2,fb:"Una media de 12 anos."},{qt:"Main concern about AI in healthcare?",o:["Electricity cost","Data privacy","Lack of computers","Too many doctors"],c:1,fb:"Privacidad de datos."},{qt:"How does AI help drug discovery?",o:["Replacing scientists","Simulating molecular interactions","Manufacturing drugs","Testing on patients"],c:1,fb:"Simula interacciones moleculares."}]},{title:"Renewable Energy Storage",text:"One of the biggest challenges in renewable energy is storage. Solar panels produce electricity during the day, but people need power at night. Wind turbines generate energy when it's windy, but calm days leave the grid short. Battery technology is crucial. Lithium-ion batteries are common but degrade over time, can overheat, and lithium mining has environmental impacts. Researchers are exploring solid-state batteries with solid electrolyte, making them safer. Flow batteries store energy in liquid solutions. Green hydrogen is also promising: excess renewable electricity splits water